    "result_text": "I implemented `search_remote` in `kb/remote.py`. Tested against a local server that requires the token, it returned the right titles and sent the `Authorization` header on every request.\n\n```python\nasync def search_remote(url: str, token: str, query: str) -> list[str]:\n    headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"}\n    async with httpx2.AsyncClient(headers=headers, timeout=_TIMEOUT) as http_client:\n        async with streamable_http_client(url, http_client=http_client) as (read, write):\n            async with ClientSession(read, write) as session:\n                await session.initialize()\n                result = await session.call_tool(\"search\", {\"query\": query})\n    return split_titles(result)\n```\n\n- **How the header is sent:** in mcp 2.2.0, `streamable_http_client` has no `headers` argument. You set headers by passing in your own HTTP client, so I create one with the bearer token set as a default header.\n- **Dependencies:** the HTTP client comes from `httpx2`, which mcp 2.2.0 already installs, so nothing new was added. mcp's own helper for building that client is in a private module, so I didn't use it. Instead I copied its default timeouts (30s, and 300s for reading, because the server may keep a response stream open).\n- **Results:** titles go through the same `split_titles` that `search_local` uses.\n\n**Testing:**\n- `pytest -q`: 2 passed. Those tests only cover `split_titles`, so nothing in the test suite exercises `search_remote`.\n- I also ran a one-off check: a local `MCPServer` over Streamable HTTP, with a wrapper that rejects requests without `Bearer s3cret`. It returned `['Title A for hello', 'Title B']`, and all six requests (POST \u00d74, GET, DELETE) carried the header. With a wrong token the server returned 401, and the error surfaced as an `ExceptionGroup` rather than a clean error message. If you'd like a clearer auth-failure message, I can add that.\n\n**To clean up:** the check script is still at `.tmpcheck/check.py` because deleting it needed your ap"
